te_q4, unit \"m³/h\"\n- q3_q1_ratio, unit null\n\nAlso add \"accuracy_class\"? It's per model, in ID. Skip.\n\nCertificate:\n{\n  \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\",\n  \"revision\": \"15\",\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"project_number\": \"4076767\",\n  \"page_total\": 13,\n  \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\"\n}\n\nHmm \"revision\" extra field. I'll include it; it's factual. Or put in number string: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01 revision 15\"? I'd rather keep separate key. Include both? No. Keep number clean + \"revision\": \"15\".\n\nrecommendation:\n{\n  \"id\": \"R49\",\n  \"edition\": 2013,\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]\n}\n\nEdition: the number \"R49/2013\" — R49 is \"2013 edition\"? R49-1:2013 confirms edition 2013. Include.\n\nmodel_family:\n{\n  \"family_name\": \"Full bore\",\n  \"models\": [ 84 entries ]\n}\n\nHmm — family_name \"Full bore\" — the tables say \"Full bore - AC mains powered\" / \"Full bore - Battery / Renewable energy powered\". \"Full bore\" is a descriptor of the meter family (vs reduced bore presumably in another part). OK.\n\nFor models[], include only model_id per compact example.\n\nNow the description text for tables:\n\n\"Flow rates Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 can be freely chosen as long as: Values Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013. Values mentioned for Q1 and Q2 are minimum values and the ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6. Values mentioned for Q3 and Q4 are maximum values and the ratio Q4/Q3 = 1.25. The ratio Q3/Q1 is at least 40.\"\n\nInclude this as description on both matrix_tables entries. Good.\n\nAlso could add \"q2_q1_ratio\": 1.6 and \"q4_q3_ratio\": 1.25 and \"q3_q1_ratio_min\": 40 as type_level characteristics? These are global conditions applying to all models. Hmm — \"The ratio Q3/Q1 is at least 40\" → characteristic \"q3_q1_ratio_min\": {value: 40}? And \"q2_over_q1_ratio\": 1.6, \"q4_over_q3_ratio\": 1.25. These are type-level (whole-cert). Rule 4 says varying attrs → model_level; these 