e extra config dim (power supply) — the model_level structure assumes a single model axis. With two power configs × sizes × classes, the model axis is a compound key, which model_level can still encode via model_id strings.\n\nGiven the explicit rule-4 emphasis and R137 precedent showing both, I'll include both matrix_tables and model_level, and models[]. I'll be careful.\n\nActually, one simplification to cut ~30%: in model_level values, use shorter model keys consistent with models[] IDs. Fine as planned.\n\nLet me also decide: should models[] entries carry attributes to disambiguate power/class? The model_id already contains \"AC mains\" / \"battery\" and \"class N\". Sufficient.\n\nHmm, actually, final sanity check on scale: maybe I'm overengineering. A human expert extracting this would probably emit matrix_tables with both tables and a modest model_family. But the R137 example literally shows model_level extraction from the same kind of table. OK go.\n\nLet me write the JSON now, being meticulous with numbers (European commas → dots).\n\nAlso \"unit_id\": for m³/h I could try \"u:cubic_metre_per_hour\" — not certain; rule says leave null unless certain. Use null everywhere for unit_id.\n\nmatrix_tables columns naming: I'll use: \"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"q1_min\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_q1_ratio\". column_units: [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null].\n\nTable names:\n1. \"Table 7 — General characteristics of the family of instruments: Full bore, AC mains powered\"\n2. \"Table 8 — General characteristics of the family of instruments: Full bore, Battery / Renewable energy powered\"\n\nNotes text (as description):\n\"Flow rates Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 can be freely chosen as long as: values Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013; values mentioned for Q1 and Q2 are minimum values and the ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6; values mentioned for Q3 and Q4 are maximum values and the ratio Q4/Q3 = 1.25; the ratio Q3/Q1 is 